  "context_pill": "Presumptive Taxation & Audit Mandate",
  "example_summary": "Mr. Praveen evaluates eligibility under Section 44AD for his retail trade, computing presumptive income, assessing the exit restriction penalty under Section 44AD(4), audit under Section 44AB, and filing due dates.",
  "source_provision": "| Provision | Description | Condition / Threshold |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Section 44AD(1) | Presumptive Income | 8% (cash) / 6% (digital) of Gross Receipts |\n| Section 44AD(4) | Exit Restriction | Mandatory 5-year cooling off period if opting out |\n| Section 44AB | Audit Mandate | Required if profit declared is less than 44AD rate |\n| Section 139(1) | Due Date | 31st July or 31st October (if audited) |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Eligibility Criteria:\n- Turnover must be less than ₹ 300 Lakhs.\n- Cash receipts must not exceed 5% of total turnover.\n- Eligible business must not include those specified under section 44AE or agency commission.\n\n> [!WARNING] Exit Restriction:\n- If an assessee opts out of section 44AD, they cannot avail the presumptive scheme for 5 consecutive assessment years. \n- During these 5 years, if total income exceeds the basic exemption limit, tax audit under section 44AB is mandatory.",
